      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Array Methods Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. map and filter",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`map(fn)` → ==new array, same length==, one transformed value per element",
                "`filter(fn)` → new array of elements where fn is **truthy**",
                "filter length can shrink to ==0==, never grows"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const nums = [1, 2, 3];",
                "nums.map(x => x * 2);     // [2, 4, 6]",
                "nums.filter(x => x > 5);  // []"
              ],
              "note": "same length vs shrunk to 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. reduce",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`reduce((acc, x) => ..., init)` folds an array into ==one value==",
                "`acc` carries the result between calls",
                "Always pass ==init==: empty array with no init throws {red:TypeError}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "[].reduce((a, x) => a + x);        // TypeError",
                "[].reduce((a, x) => a + x, 0);     // 0",
                "[1, 2, 3].reduce((a, x) => a + x, 0);  // 6"
              ],
              "note": "init is also the result for an empty array"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mutation and chaining",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Returns",
                "Mutates original"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`map`",
                  "new array",
                  "{green:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "`filter`",
                  "new array",
                  "{green:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "`reduce`",
                  "one value",
                  "{green:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "`forEach`",
                  "`undefined`",
                  "{green:no}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "forEach cannot chain",
              "text": "`forEach` returns ==undefined==, so `.forEach(...).map(...)` crashes. Use map/filter to chain."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Searching, Testing and Sorting",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Searching, Testing and Sorting",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Find and Test",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Returns",
                "On empty array"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`find(fn)`",
                  "first match or ==undefined==",
                  "undefined"
                ],
                [
                  "`findIndex(fn)`",
                  "its index or ==-1==",
                  "-1"
                ],
                [
                  "`some(fn)`",
                  "true if **at least one** passes",
                  "{red:false}"
                ],
                [
                  "`every(fn)`",
                  "true only if **all** pass",
                  "{green:true}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`some` and `every` ==short-circuit==: they stop at the first decisive element",
                "`every` on `[]` is vacuously **true**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sorting",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`sort()` with no comparator compares **as strings**",
                "Numbers need a comparator: `(a,b) => a-b` ascending"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "[10,9,1].sort()            // [1, 10, 9]",
                "[10,9,1].sort((a,b) => a-b) // [1, 9, 10]"
              ],
              "note": "default order is string order"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`sort` ==mutates in place== and returns the **same reference**",
                "Copy first, then sort"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const s1 = [...arr].sort((a,b) => a-b)",
                "const s2 = arr.toSorted((a,b) => a-b)"
              ],
              "note": "arr stays unchanged"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Always pass `(a,b) => a-b` for numbers, and never sort the original array you still need."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Spread and Destructuring",
      "role": "outline",
