    {
      "title": "Shallow vs Deep Copy and structuredClone",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Shallow vs Deep Copy and structuredClone",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Shallow Copies",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`b = a` copies the ==reference==, not the data; mutating b also mutates a",
                "Spread, `Object.assign`, `slice`, `Array.from` make ==shallow== copies",
                "Top level is new; {red:nested objects are still shared}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const o = { inner: { x: 0 } };",
                "const c = { ...o };",
                "c.inner.x = 1;",
                "console.log(o.inner.x); // 1"
              ],
              "note": "the shallow copy trap: o.inner is shared"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Deep Copy",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`structuredClone(value)` is a true ==deep copy==",
                "Handles Date, Map, Set, RegExp and **circular references**",
                "Drops class prototypes and getters",
                "`JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(x))` is a {orange:lossy} deep copy"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "structuredClone",
                "JSON round-trip"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Date",
                  "kept",
                  "string"
                ],
                [
                  "Map/Set",
                  "kept",
                  "{} (contents lost)"
                ],
                [
                  "undefined",
                  "kept",
                  "dropped"
                ],
                [
                  "Functions",
                  "{red:throws}",
                  "dropped"
                ],
                [
                  "Circular",
                  "{green:OK}",
                  "{red:throws}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Functions",
              "text": "`structuredClone` throws ==DataCloneError== on functions. Spread copies only one level."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Object.entries and Map/Set vs Plain Objects",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Object.entries and Map/Set vs Plain Objects",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Entries Round Trip",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Object.entries(obj)== returns `[key, value]` pairs of own enumerable **string** keys",
                "`Object.keys` gives keys only; `Object.values` gives values only"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const obj = { a: 1, b: 2 };",
                "Object.fromEntries(",
                "  Object.entries(obj).map(([k, v]) => [k, v*2])",
                ");"
              ],
              "note": "result { a: 2, b: 4 }: every value transformed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Map vs Plain Object",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Map",
                "Object"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Keys",
                  "**any** type: objects, functions, `NaN`",
                  "coerced to string or symbol"
                ],
                [
                  "Order",
                  "insertion order",
                  "string keys, coerced"
                ],
                [
                  "Size",
                  "`.size`",
                  "`Object.keys(o).length`"
                ],
                [
                  "Iterate",
                  "directly iterable",
                  "via `Object.entries(o)`"
                ],
                [
                  "API",
                  "`.get .set .has .delete`",
                  "inherits `toString` etc."
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Set",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Set== stores **unique** values",
                "`[...new Set(arr)]` dedupes an array",
                "`set.has(x)` is ==O(1)==; `arr.includes(x)` is O(n)"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Which to Pick",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Use",
                "When"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Plain object",
                  "fixed-shape records, JSON"
                ],
                [
                  "Map",
                  "dynamic keys, non-string keys, frequent add and delete"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Key coercion",
              "text": "`obj[{}]` silently uses the key `\"[object Object]\"`. A Map keeps the ==object itself== as the key."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
